TASK: Enforce strict sequential slip numbering across the whole ERP, add an optional "void slip" path, and make every receiving source use the same sequence check.

CONTEXT
Slip Sequences mirror physical paper books (book_start_no to book_end_no, current_slip_no, used_count). Receiving slips (Model 19 / GRN) and outgoing slips (SIN) are currently created in several places. Relevant files: SlipSequenceController.php, SlipSequence.php, StoreManagerController.php (slip + void logic), ProcurementLifecycleService.php (Stage 9 store intake), and the transfers flow.

1. STRICT SEQUENCE RULE (no skipping)
- A slip number may only be accepted if it equals the store's next expected number (current_slip_no). Example: slip 2103 must be rejected if 2102 has not been used or voided.
- This applies to manual entry and auto-fill alike. Remove the old behavior that "jumps" the counter past a manually entered number.
- If a number is higher than expected, reject with a clear message that lists every missing number, e.g. "Slip 2103 can't be saved. 2101 and 2102 are not recorded yet. Record or void them first."
- If a number is lower than expected or already used, reject as a duplicate.
- A number outside book_start_no..book_end_no is rejected. When the book is full, block saving and prompt "Next Book".
- Enforce this in ONE place: a SlipSequenceService method, e.g. consumeNext(store_id, type, number), that runs inside a DB transaction with lockForUpdate() on the sequence row, so two storekeepers cannot take the same number at the same time.
- Add a unique index on (store_id, slip_type, slip_no) as a database-level guard.

2. OPTIONAL VOID SLIP
- Voiding is optional, never automatic. A storekeeper can void the next expected slip (spoiled, torn, cancelled paper) so the sequence can move on.
- When a higher number is rejected, show a "Void missing slips" action listing the missing numbers, so the user can void them in one step and then save the slip they wanted.
- Void requires a reason (required text field) and permission check. Record who voided it and when.
- A void slip: counts as used in the sequence, creates NO stock movement, reverses any stock effect if it was previously posted, and shows as a red/void leaf on the leaf map.
- Voided numbers can never be reused.

3. RECEIVABLE SLIP SOURCES (all must use the same service)
Every receivable slip must call SlipSequenceService, never write numbers on its own:
  a) Purchase intake: Stage 9 Store Intake on a Purchase Request. Pre-fill the next number from /api/slip-sequences/{store_id}/receive and validate on submit.
  b) Petty cash purchase: add a receive path for items bought with petty cash (no PR or supplier PO). Add source_type = "petty_cash" on the receipt, link it to the petty cash voucher or expense record, take a GRN number from the store's active receiving sequence, and increase stock through InventoryService.
  c) Transfer receipt: when the destination store receives a transfer, record the receiving slip (receiving_slip_no) from the destination store's sequence. The outgoing slip (SIN / waybill) uses the origin store's outgoing sequence.
- Keep a source_type column (procurement, petty_cash, transfer_in, transfer_out, manual) on the receipt so the leaf map and history can show where each slip came from.

4. CROSS-CHECK ACROSS ALL SOURCES
- Receipts from purchase intake, petty cash, and transfers share the same book per store, so numbers must be continuous across all three.
- Add a reconciliation check per sequence that verifies: every number from book_start_no to current_slip_no - 1 is either used (with a source) or void; no duplicates; no gaps; used_count matches the actual rows.
- Add a "Cross-check" button on the Slip Sequence details page and a section in Slip History that shows OK / problems per book, with the list of any gap numbers or mismatches.
- Include a one-off command or migration check that scans existing data and reports old gaps or duplicates without changing them.

5. UI CHANGES
- Slips page, PR Stage 9, petty cash receive form, and transfer receive form: show "Next slip: NNNN" and block submit with an inline error when the number is wrong.
- Leaf map colors: green = GRN (purchase), indigo = transfer, teal = petty cash, blue = next, red = void, yellow = gap (legacy only), gray = available.

6. TESTS (write them)
- Accepting 2102 before 2101 is rejected; after voiding 2101 it is accepted.
- Duplicate number rejected; out-of-range rejected.
- Two simultaneous requests for the same number: only one succeeds.
- Void creates no stock change and reverses stock if posted.
- Petty cash, PR intake, and transfer receipts all advance the same counter.
- Reconciliation reports a deliberately created gap.

DELIVERABLES
Migration(s), SlipSequenceService, controller and form updates, the reconciliation check, tests, and a short summary of every file changed. Do not remove existing slip history data.